3. Summary
3.1. Summary: formation of conical liquid film
A lot of researches have focused on the formation of conical liquid film, especially the formation of air core, the growth of boundary layer, the film thickness, the discharge coefficient and the growth of disturbance on the gas liquid interface. These researches are really thorough. However the research on the unstable air core is limited, the mechanism of the double-helical air core is not clear. Thus the unsteady internal flow characteristics should be focused on in the future.
3.2. Summary: breakup of conical liquid film
Research on the breakup of the conical liquid film mainly focus on the spray pattern, the spray cone angle and the breakup length. However, the research, especially the experimental research, on the surface waves which lead to the breakup of the conical liquid film is limited. Only several papers report the investigation on the surface waves with the linear stability analysis.
3.3. Summary: atomization characteristics of the conical liquid film
The atomization characteristics of pressure swirl injector are mainly obtained from experimental research, because the breakup and atomization of the conical liquid film is very complicate and is very hard to simulate. Researches on the atomization characteristics mainly focus on the SMD and the mean axial velocity distributions, and the researches on the diameter-velocity distribution and the mass flow rate distribution are limited.
3.4. Summary: effects of the rocket engine environment
The rocket engine environment includes the high back pressure and temperature. The back pressure promotes the atomization because it increases the gas density and enhances the gas liquid interaction. High temperature and high pressure may change the propellants from subcritical to supercritical condition. Once the supercritical condition is achieved, the surface tension and the latent heat of evaporation become zero. Thus the combustion is dominated by the mixing state of the propellants. Above all, high back pressure and temperature are good for atomization.
3.5. Summary: response of injector and atomization on the pressure oscillation
The effects of pressure oscillation on the injection and atomization has been investigated for a long time, but researches mainly focus on the injector dynamics. A lot of thorough theoretical, numerical and experimental researches have been conducted, and the response characteristics of the pressure swirl injector have well understood. However, the injector dynamics mainly focus on the response of the mass flow rate at the injector exit on the pressure oscillation in supply system. The effects of the pressure oscillation on the primary breakup and atomization characteristics have not been well researched. The response characteristics of the primary breakup and secondary atomization on the pressure oscillation is still needed.
4. Conclusion
To ensure the reliability and stability of the liquid rocket engine, the configuration of the pressure swirl injector used in liquid rocket engines should be as simple as possible. Thus the pressure swirl injector with tangential inlet ports is widely used in liquid rocket engine. Commonly, this type of pressure swirl injector consists of tangential inlet ports, a swirl chamber, a converging spin chamber, and a discharge orifice. And it can be further divided into converge-end swirl injector and open-end swirl injector based on whether there is a converging spin chamber. The atomization of the liquid propellants includes the formation of liquid film, primary breakup and secondary atomization. And the back pressure and temperature in the combustion chamber could have great influence on the atomization of the injector. What's more, when the combustion instability occurs, the pressure oscillation could further affects the atomization process. This paper reviewed the atomization mechanism and the performance of the pressure swirl injector, which include the formation of the conical liquid film, the breakup of the conical liquid film, the atomization characteristics of the conical liquid film, the effects of the rocket engine environment, and the response of the injector and atomization on the pressure oscillation.
